  "statement": "At fixed cutoff and positive floor, the exact R-147 fresh final scalar innovation cannot be a nonzero final block of the R-146 proportional-covariance canonical chart: the registered active-spectator covariance restriction is positive definite, so every nonzero canonical block has rank two, whereas the fresh line innovation has rank one. A rank-one past block is only a no-correction fixture, not a necessity for an adapted past. This does not obstruct a new full-rank canonical chart. In a separately declared noncanonical last-root Gaussian coefficient completion, the predictable trace-bracket mismatch is exactly delta=-sigma^4 E f''(sigma g)+sigma^4||E A'(sigma g)||^2 and, at each fixed point strictly inside the R-147 adverse region, is positive for all sufficiently small sigma. For the coefficient-background parameter family q=m+sigma g with current prefactor sigma g held fixed, the uncentred owner is sigma^4 E f''/2, its parameter gradient uses f''', and its parameter Hessian uses f''''. This is not a physical deterministic-control Hessian because no source synthesis is specified. The fourth-derivative threshold is R^2/e=-3/14+3sqrt(11)/28, strictly below the R-147 threshold; hence at each fixed adverse point the pointwise small-noise owner and terminal-sextic curvature are positive, the source curvature is nonnegative, and the parameter gradient is nonzero (negative in the oriented convention R>0). The coefficient diagonal does not identify the full forest/future/balanced/low/spatial owner. No phase is selected.",
